    "kfPrivacy.intro": "Keyframe is a photo cleanup app published by Mertcan Çezik. It does not require an account, registration or login, and it has no servers that receive your photos.",
    "kfPrivacy.photosHeading": "Your photos and videos",
    "kfPrivacy.photos1": "Keyframe reads only the photos and videos you allow in your phone’s photo permission. You can allow your whole library or selected items and change this at any time in your phone’s settings.",
    "kfPrivacy.photos2": "To show your library, group similar shots, find blurry and dark photos and large videos, Keyframe looks at your photos, their dates, albums and file sizes on your device. Photos, videos and the results of these checks are never uploaded or shared by Keyframe.",
    "kfPrivacy.photos3": "Keyframe deletes items only after you confirm. On iPhone they move to Recently Deleted in the Photos app, and your phone asks for its own confirmation. On Android they move to the system trash where your Android version supports it.",
    "kfPrivacy.deviceHeading": "Data stored on your device",
    "kfPrivacy.device1": "Keyframe stores your review progress, keep and delete decisions, review history, photos waiting to be deleted, your daily deletion count and settings on your device. There is no cloud sync, no advertising, no behavioral analytics and no tracking.",
    "kfPrivacy.device2": "On iPhone, Keyframe saves the start time of its welcome offer in the Keychain so the offer does not restart if the app is reinstalled. This entry holds only a date and time and may remain on your device after you delete the app.",
    "kfPrivacy.purchaseHeading": "Purchases",
    "kfPrivacy.purchase1": "To show plans, complete or restore purchases and check Pro access, Keyframe connects to the Apple App Store and RevenueCat, its purchase service. They process an anonymous app user identifier and your purchase history to deliver Pro and to analyze purchases. Keyframe does not ask for or store your name, email address or payment details.",
    "kfPrivacy.purchase2": "Purchase records are managed by your App Store account. Refunds and billing questions are handled by Apple.",
    "kfPrivacy.retentionHeading": "Retention and deletion",
    "kfPrivacy.retention": "Data Keyframe keeps in its own storage is removed when you delete the app. Your photos stay in your library unless you choose to delete them. Purchase records are kept by Apple and RevenueCat. Because Keyframe has no account, there is no profile to delete.",
    "kfPrivacy.contact": "For questions about this policy, please", "kfPrivacy.supportLink": "contact Keyframe support",
    "kfTerms.meta": "Terms version: 1.0 · Last updated: 24 November 2026",
    "kfTerms.p1": "Keyframe is published by Mertcan Çezik and provided for personal use to review and clean up your own photo library. The app is provided as-is.",
    "kfTerms.p2": "You decide what to delete. Keyframe deletes items only after you confirm, and they first move to your phone’s Recently Deleted album or trash, where they can be recovered for a limited time, usually 30 days. After that they are removed by your phone. Please keep a backup of photos you care about. Keyframe is not responsible for items you choose to delete.",
    "kfTerms.p3": "The free plan lets you review as many photos as you like and delete up to 20 a day. Keyframe Pro removes the daily limit and adds similar-shot, blurry-photo, video and largest-photo cleanup, and suggests the best shot in each group. These checks are estimates; always look before you delete.",
    "kfTerms.p4": "Pro is sold through the Apple App Store as a yearly or monthly subscription or a one-time lifetime purchase. Subscriptions renew automatically unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the end of the current period, and you can manage them in your App Store account settings. If a free trial is offered, it turns into a paid subscription when it ends unless you cancel before then. A lifetime purchase does not renew. New users may see a limited-time welcome offer.",
    "kfTerms.p5": "The App Store shows the price and applicable taxes before you buy. Refunds, billing disputes and payment details are handled by Apple. Use Restore purchases to get Pro on another device with the same Apple account.",
    "kfTerms.p6": "For help, please", "kfTerms.supportLink": "contact Keyframe support",
    "kfSupport.meta": "Support · Updated 24 November 2026 · Published by Mertcan Çezik.",
    "kfSupport.intro": "If Keyframe is not working as expected, email us. Include the app version, your device and a short description of the issue.",
