    "kfSupport.faqHeading": "Common questions",
    "kfSupport.q1": "Where do deleted photos go?", "kfSupport.a1": "To Recently Deleted in the Photos app. You can restore them there for about 30 days. After that your iPhone removes them for good.",
    "kfSupport.q2": "Keyframe does not show all my photos.", "kfSupport.a2": "You may have allowed only selected photos. Go to Settings → Apps → Keyframe → Photos and choose Full Access, or add more photos there.",
    "kfSupport.q3": "How do I get Pro on a new phone?", "kfSupport.a3": "Sign in with the same Apple account, open Settings → Keyframe Pro in the app and tap Restore purchases.",
    "kfSupport.q4": "Why can I only delete 20 photos a day?", "kfSupport.a4": "That is the free plan’s daily limit. It resets every day. Pro removes the limit, and photos you marked stay saved until you can delete them.",
